WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.740
I was hoping that you were up.

00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:22.719
Is everything all right?

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:26.760
It's about Jason.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.120
I think I've made a horrible mistake.

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:32.980
Jason.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:38.840
Lana, I'm not sure I'm the one you should be talking to about this.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.200
Actually, I think that you're exactly who I should be talking to.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.719
I've been thinking about it.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.780
The way we met, the way he followed me here, the way he got a job at my school.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.900
I think that everything that Jason has told me has been a lie.

00:00:56.759 --> 00:01:01.719
I'm starting to wonder if there's another reason why he came to Smallville besides me.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:03.640
Like what?

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:04.739
I don't know.

00:01:07.379 --> 00:01:09.579
But he's really starting to scare me.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.159
Don't worry, Lana.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.959
I'd never let anything happen to you.

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:16.900
I know.

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:21.379
And it's made one thing very clear.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:26.659
I never should have given up on it.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:34.400
I can lie to myself as much as I want, but I've always been in love with you.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.480
I can.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.020
I don't know.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:37.480
I don't know.

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:38.960
I can't tell you that I've been in love with you.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:40.719
I know.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:49.640
But I've always been in love with you.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.280
I know.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.080
I can't.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:55.380
I can't.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:55.540
I can't.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.740
I can't.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:06.600
I knew I couldn't trust you, Clark.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:07.900
Jason, no!

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.040
Haven't you hurt her enough already?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.159
Jason!

00:02:26.759 --> 00:02:37.280
Clark can't protect you from me.

00:02:38.579 --> 00:02:39.560
Nobody can.

00:02:56.759 --> 00:03:14.819
Jason!

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:14.979
Jason!

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:23.280
Someone call an ambulance!

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:25.979
Jason.

00:03:26.759 --> 00:03:27.939
Jason, can you hear me?

00:03:27.939 --> 00:03:28.000
I can.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.500
I know.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:38.439
Somebody save me

00:03:38.439 --> 00:03:43.319
Let your war hands break right through

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:48.379
Somebody save me

00:03:48.379 --> 00:03:53.959
Don't care how you do it

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:55.659
Just stay

00:03:55.659 --> 00:03:56.739
Stay

00:03:56.759 --> 00:04:00.199
Come on

00:04:00.199 --> 00:04:04.539
I've been waiting for you

00:04:04.539 --> 00:04:14.500
I've made this whole world shine for you

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.719
Stay

00:04:15.719 --> 00:04:18.219
Stay

00:04:18.219 --> 00:04:20.079
Come on

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:31.360
forget it

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.099
I know you'll never make it

00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:34.579
You'll never forget it

00:04:34.579 --> 00:04:38.019
Sorry I should never make it

00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:39.879
But I'm Vicar II

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.539
Your Role��

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:45.639
1899

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:46.899
Mr. Martin

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:56.699
I didn't know you?

00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:59.459
The doctors don't know.

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:02.819
His heart's beating a mile a minute,

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.300
and they can't get his blood pressure down.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:08.180
That's a little odd for someone who's unconscious, isn't it?

00:05:09.219 --> 00:05:11.379
Well, he said he's in some sort of a panic mode,

00:05:11.839 --> 00:05:13.839
like he's having a severe nightmare.

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:18.599
What happened?

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:27.520
He came by the town to pick me up for lunch,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.580
and I ran upstairs to grab a jacket.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:32.340
And?

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.220
And I heard a crash.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.780
That's it.

00:05:41.939 --> 00:05:44.439
He's been perfectly healthy.

00:05:45.439 --> 00:05:48.580
But the doctors say that if they can't get his heart rate up,

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.879
he'll get down, and then he could have a heart attack.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.439
They must have some idea of what caused this.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:58.840
I wish I could help them.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.200
But he was just studying all morning before he came to the apartment.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.820
The first time I saw him, he was lying on the town floor.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.200
Well, let us know if there's anything we can do to help, okay?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:13.280
Okay.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.580
They need his insurance.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.040
His card.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.060
It's in my apartment.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.660
Could you guys go get it for me?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:23.879
I don't want to leave his side.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:24.320
Yeah.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.060
Okay.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:25.140
Okay.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.060
Clark, I don't mean to go all Dr. Phil on you,

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.060
but don't you think you should admit

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.580
that they're in a relationship?

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.080
But I don't think they're in a relationship.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.160
Come on, Chloe, I'm past that.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:55.820
Yeah, I should have known by that crippling stare on your face

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.080
ever since you walked in the apartment.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.360
I just could have used some more time to ease into it, yeah?

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.120
Clark, you were in love with her.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.640
That's not something you just ease out of.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.260
Just by the time that I found out,

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.100
they were already this serious thing.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:12.120
Yeah.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.840
But we all keep secrets for our own reasons.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.920
I don't think I have to tell you that.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:27.020
I don't think going through Jason's personal things falls under your snoop jurisdiction.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.080
I'll take my chances with the jury on this one.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.340
I think maybe if we backtrack through Jason's last couple of days, it might help.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:35.000
Oh.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.460
Jason had a meeting at Luther Corp this morning.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:41.820
Why didn't Lana say something?

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:43.640
Maybe she didn't know.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:53.860
This place seems dead.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:54.500
Yeah.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.340
My dad used to work the overtime shifts on Saturdays.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.800
This lot should be full by now.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.160
Where do you think everybody is?

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:05.020
I don't know.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.160
But while you're talking to Lex, I'm going to get myself a little backstage tour.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:26.700
Clark?

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.200
How the hell did you get in here?

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.519
Yeah, the gate was open.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.659
Your security seems a little MIA lately.

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:37.600
That's obvious, but this is a restricted area.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:38.800
This will only take a second.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.420
I need someone to escort a guest out.

00:08:44.779 --> 00:08:46.639
Look, Clark, I'm sorry, but I just got in from Metropolis.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.460
I got a lot to do.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:48.500
Just now.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.860
I thought you had a meeting with Jason this morning.

00:08:52.639 --> 00:08:53.279
Not with me.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.980
He was meeting with the head of my HR department.

00:08:56.019 --> 00:08:56.899
You giving him a job?

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:58.980
Just some leads.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.259
I felt guilty for getting Jason fired from the school.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:04.960
He didn't even want Lana to know about it.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:05.960
I'm surprised he told you.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:06.500
He didn't.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.300
Jason's lying unconscious at the hospital.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.820
Some sort of neurological stress.

00:09:13.639 --> 00:09:14.540
Do they know what happened?

00:09:15.279 --> 00:09:15.680
No.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.580
But your HR guy might have been the last person to know.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.139
I don't think he's the right person to talk to.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.060
Look, I'll track him down, but Clark,

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.899
there could be a lot of reasons for Jason's condition.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:25.960
There could also be a lot of reasons

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.480
why this place is deserted halfway through Saturday's shift.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.379
I'll call in a specialist from Metropolis to take a look at him.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.860
I'm sure Lana and I are doing everything I can for him.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:19.940
I know, jailhouse, protocols.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:20.460
Take care.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:22.560
You and Forces.

00:10:22.639 --> 00:10:23.480
Get out what it's worth.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.100
But why did we create the Bypass?!

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:30.639
But, right now!

00:10:30.779 --> 00:10:33.540
Why do you think this trouble might have happened?!

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.940
I thought I was fundamentally lost!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.360
Umm...

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.660
Let me explain.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:48.440
Lala has again been going Chapter 10 over.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:11:13.600
I've been waiting for you, Chloe.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:15.820
Mom?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.700
You can't escape this, Chloe.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.259
None of the women in our family ever have.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.519
There'll be no ending for Chloe unless we do something.

00:11:52.519 --> 00:11:53.899
Jojo?

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:54.980
Just like we always do.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.360
No.

00:11:56.399 --> 00:11:58.320
No.

00:11:58.779 --> 00:12:00.240
No, I won't!

00:12:00.659 --> 00:12:05.820
Chloe?

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:12.620
No, no, no, no, no!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.500
No!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.580
Do you not see it?

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.720
No!

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:18.300
No!

00:12:48.600 --> 00:13:01.120
No way coming.

00:13:10.279 --> 00:13:12.200
With all our safety precautions,

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.920
how the hell does a lab explode?

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.000
Well, when you're dealing with meteor rocks,

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.720
it's very difficult to predict how our chemicals will react.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.100
Mr. Luther, we're doing everything we can.

00:13:26.279 --> 00:13:28.299
After the alarm sounded, we sealed the room.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.220
All affected personnel have been quarantined,

00:13:31.279 --> 00:13:32.940
and we're trying to fix the damaged pipes.

00:13:34.259 --> 00:13:36.240
You mean the bacteria is still leaking out?

00:13:36.679 --> 00:13:37.700
Only in that room.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.799
Once the situation is under control,

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.840
I want the project dismantled.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.299
But, Mr. Luther,

00:13:47.299 --> 00:13:50.659
your father negotiated this contract with the military.

00:13:50.659 --> 00:13:53.859
We stand to make a lot if we can ever market the compound.

00:13:53.859 --> 00:13:56.359
And exactly what is the market for toxins

00:13:56.359 --> 00:13:58.559
that invoke a person's worst nightmare

00:13:58.559 --> 00:14:00.559
before they fall unconscious, Dr. Ford?

00:14:00.559 --> 00:14:01.559
Think of the good.

00:14:01.559 --> 00:14:03.559
I mean, we could disable the enemy

00:14:03.559 --> 00:14:04.559
without ever using violence.

00:14:04.559 --> 00:14:06.059
We have statistics to prove...

00:14:06.059 --> 00:14:08.059
Statistics aren't lying in those beds.

00:14:08.059 --> 00:14:09.059
My employees are.

00:14:11.059 --> 00:14:13.059
And I'm afraid they're not the only ones.

00:14:14.059 --> 00:14:15.059
What do you mean?

00:14:15.059 --> 00:14:16.039
I'm afraid they're not the only ones.

00:14:16.039 --> 00:14:17.039
What do you mean?

00:14:17.299 --> 00:14:19.299
Someone who was visiting the plant this morning

00:14:19.299 --> 00:14:21.299
is at the hospital right now with the same symptoms.

00:14:22.799 --> 00:14:23.799
Is he contagious?

00:14:23.799 --> 00:14:25.299
Oh, no, sir. No, sir.

00:14:25.299 --> 00:14:27.299
I mean, the bacteria can't be transmitted

00:14:27.299 --> 00:14:28.299
from one person to another.

00:14:28.299 --> 00:14:29.799
It has to be inhaled directly.

00:14:29.799 --> 00:14:31.299
Then there's no need to call the CDC

00:14:31.299 --> 00:14:33.299
and panic the entire town.

00:14:33.799 --> 00:14:35.799
Now, where are we with the antidote?

00:14:37.299 --> 00:14:41.299
This will clarify when it reaches 1,000 degrees Kelvin.

00:14:41.299 --> 00:14:42.799
And then we can test it.

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:44.299
What's the ETA?

00:14:47.299 --> 00:14:50.299
Another five hours.

00:14:56.299 --> 00:14:58.299
Eight other people have just come down

00:14:58.299 --> 00:15:00.299
with the condition that Jason and Chloe have.

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:03.299
The doctors haven't found anything in common?

00:15:03.299 --> 00:15:05.299
Didn't you say that Jason and Chloe

00:15:05.299 --> 00:15:06.299
were both at Luther Corp today?

00:15:06.299 --> 00:15:08.299
Yeah, but half of the victims at the hospital weren't.

00:15:09.299 --> 00:15:12.299
Whatever this is seems to strike completely at random.

00:15:12.299 --> 00:15:14.299
There's no way to tell who's gonna be next.

00:15:14.299 --> 00:15:16.299
That sounds contagious in the air or the water.

00:15:16.299 --> 00:15:19.299
Maybe it'll show up in some environmental quality report.

00:15:23.299 --> 00:15:25.299
Lana, come on in.

00:15:26.299 --> 00:15:27.299
Um...

00:15:28.299 --> 00:15:29.299
Sorry to show up like this.

00:15:29.299 --> 00:15:31.299
I just didn't know where else to go.

00:15:31.299 --> 00:15:33.299
Clark told us about Jason.

00:15:33.299 --> 00:15:34.299
Has something happened?

00:15:34.299 --> 00:15:37.299
One of the other infected people just died.

00:15:38.299 --> 00:15:41.299
Lana, do the doctors have any idea at all what's going on?

00:15:42.299 --> 00:15:45.299
Just that a person's body can only sustain a level of oxygen.

00:15:46.299 --> 00:15:49.299
A level of panic for so long before their heart gives out.

00:15:52.299 --> 00:15:53.299
I can't...

00:15:53.299 --> 00:15:55.299
I can't just sit in that hospital anymore.

00:15:55.299 --> 00:15:56.299
Just...

00:15:56.299 --> 00:15:59.299
Just watching Chloe and Jason die.

00:16:03.299 --> 00:16:05.299
I want to help.

00:16:16.299 --> 00:16:18.299
I hope I didn't separate you from your flock.

00:16:18.299 --> 00:16:20.299
I understand your cynicism, Word and Stone,

00:16:20.299 --> 00:16:22.299
but I assure you I truly am a changed man.

00:16:22.299 --> 00:16:24.299
Oh, just a smart one.

00:16:24.299 --> 00:16:26.299
Ever since you proclaimed this sudden conversion to our residence, St. Paul,

00:16:26.299 --> 00:16:28.299
there hasn't been a single attempt on your life.

00:16:28.299 --> 00:16:30.299
I want only to be of help to others.

00:16:30.299 --> 00:16:32.299
What is the value of helping others?

00:16:32.299 --> 00:16:34.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:34.299 --> 00:16:36.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:36.299 --> 00:16:38.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:38.299 --> 00:16:40.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:42.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:42.299 --> 00:16:44.299
I want to be of help to others.

00:16:44.299 --> 00:16:47.299
What is the value of my sinful life

00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:51.299
unless I use it as an example to shepherd fellow sinners,

00:16:51.299 --> 00:16:55.299
to lead them away from the allure of hedonism and mistrust and greed,

00:16:55.299 --> 00:16:57.299
to follow a better way?

00:16:58.299 --> 00:17:00.299
Uh-huh.

00:17:00.299 --> 00:17:03.299
Well, I'm afraid you're going to have to change congregations.

00:17:03.299 --> 00:17:04.299
What do you mean?

00:17:04.299 --> 00:17:06.299
The appellate court overturned your conviction.

00:17:06.299 --> 00:17:08.299
Overturned?

00:17:08.299 --> 00:17:10.299
My appeal doesn't come up for months.

00:17:10.299 --> 00:17:11.299
It's not possible.

00:17:11.299 --> 00:17:14.299
Now, you'd be surprised what's possible in this judiciary.

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:17.299
You know, I've done everything to work this system.

00:17:17.299 --> 00:17:19.299
I hired the best lawyers in the world.

00:17:19.299 --> 00:17:23.299
I tried to pay off everyone from the bailiff to the president of the United States,

00:17:23.299 --> 00:17:25.299
and I was told, categorically,

00:17:25.299 --> 00:17:28.299
I was never going to see life outside these walls again.

00:17:28.299 --> 00:17:31.299
You do not want to be telling me things of this nature.

00:17:31.299 --> 00:17:32.299
Yes, I do.

00:17:32.299 --> 00:17:34.299
I'm guilty.

00:17:34.299 --> 00:17:37.299
Not of the crime I've been in prison for, but...

00:17:40.299 --> 00:17:42.299
So, my appeal is to you.

00:17:42.299 --> 00:17:45.299
So many other crimes.

00:17:45.299 --> 00:17:48.299
We should have landed me in here years ago.

00:17:49.299 --> 00:17:51.299
This is where I belong.

00:17:51.299 --> 00:17:53.299
It's where I can do the most good.

00:17:56.299 --> 00:17:57.299
You...

00:17:58.299 --> 00:18:00.299
You wanted to stay in prison?

00:18:02.299 --> 00:18:04.299
Yes, I do.

00:18:04.299 --> 00:18:06.299
I've found my...

00:18:10.299 --> 00:18:11.299
my mission in life.

00:18:12.299 --> 00:18:13.299
And you went on a mission?

00:18:13.299 --> 00:18:14.299
Yes, it's a motto of mine.

00:18:14.299 --> 00:18:17.299
What do you mean that you can go into prison instead of trying to kill yourself?

00:18:17.299 --> 00:18:20.799
It's not only that you want to hold on tight in there,

00:18:21.299 --> 00:18:22.680
it's also that you want to keep it a secret

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:23.299
and never give up.

00:18:23.299 --> 00:18:24.299
You think I'd cover yourself for what I just did.

00:18:24.299 --> 00:18:25.299
Yes, I did.

00:18:27.299 --> 00:18:28.299
